{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MH4KJokAtFV36pgDwd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm test` and `npm run size` pass\n\nAdoption now stays aligned after a `raw()` value with several top-level nodes. All five checklist items are done and committed.\n\n**Cause:** the old walker treated each node parsed from `raw()` as its own item and skipped whitespace and comments before each one. A whitespace text node inside the raw content therefore consumed the next real element. Every later item was then off by one, so a following button lost its listener and a \"missing node\" warning was logged.\n\n**Fix:** the change is in the parsed-node branch of `_adopt` in `src/htm.browser.ts`.\n1. Each parsed raw node now uses up exactly one DOM node.\n2. Skipping happens only before the first node of the raw content. The first node is the one with no previous sibling in its parsed fragment.\n3. That skipping stops at the first DOM node of the same type as the raw content's first node, so raw content that starts with whitespace text or a comment isn't skipped over.\n\n`_items` needed no change, and server output for `raw()` is untouched.\n\n**Tests:** two new adoption tests in `test/index.ts`:\n- Two elements separated by a newline, then a button: its `onclick` fires.\n- Text and elements (`hi <b>a</b> <i>c</i>`), then a bound attribute: it updates when the signal changes.\n\nBoth tests also check that no warning is logged and that adoption changes nothing in the DOM. I ran both against the old code and they failed there. The first version of the second test (`hi <b>a</b>` with no inner whitespace) passed on the old code too, so I added the whitespace to make it a real test.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npm test`: 292/292 pass.\n- `npm run test:ssr`: 79/79 pass, exact-string assertions unchanged.\n- `npm run size`: the browser templater is at 4.58 kB of its 4.6 kB limit, so the limit and ADR-007 stay as they are. Only 0.02 kB is left for the other adoption tickets.\n- Lint is clean.\n\nI also added a short note on how `raw()` content is adopted to the browser templater section of AGENTS.md. Notes for this attempt are in `.nightralph/notes.md` (not committed). One thing for whoever runs tests next: another worktree's `npm test` briefly held port 8123, so a run can fail with `EADDRINUSE`, and simply retrying works."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":312,"cache_read_input_tokens":72580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":312},"output_tokens":707,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae342065-041e-4af0-b0b5-d73a2a5cfea6","uuid":"3494c8a6-6b83-4e62-b38c-c9f5d04b8c98","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:57:06.608Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MH42wpDaoCmg5q7QcB"}
